    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9282": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Arts &amp; Science - Postdoctoral Fellow (Department of Philosophy)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Arts &amp; Science - Postdoctoral Fellow (Department of Philosophy) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty of Arts & Science - Postdoctoral Fellow (Department of Philosophy) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Faculty of Arts & Science - Postdoctoral Fellow (Department of Philosophy) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Tenure Information Not Applicable Position Details Position Details Dr. Katharina Stevens is offering a full-time, 18-month Postdoctoral Fellowship in Argumentation Theory, with a start date of January 1 or July 1, 2027, to be carried out in person at the University of Lethbridge. The successful candidate will have a PhD in Philosophy or a closely related area, with a background in argumentation theory or a related area and will be interested in working on topics related to voice, silencing, or standing in argumentation. This Fellowship offers the opportunity to gain significant experience in academic editing, as well as to engage in both research and teaching. The successful candidate will be a Postdoctoral Fellow with, and have the opportunity to engage in the activities of, the Critical Thinking and Civic Engagement ( CTCE ) Lab and the Department of Philosophy at the University of Lethbridge. Fellowship Details The successful candidate will: Be available to work in person, in Lethbridge, starting January 1 or July 1 2027 and continuing for the 18 months following that date. Participate in the organization of a workshop on, and serve as one of three editors of a planned edited collection on the topic of, “Voice and Standing in Argumentation,” for which they will have an opportunity to contribute a chapter (subject to review). Conduct their own research. Teach one course per academic term (3 total). Support the Informal Logic editorial team and copy-editing team. Develop a special issue policy and a social media strategy for Informal Logic, to be presented to and discussed with the editorial team. The Supervisor and/or University will offer: A salary of $47,000.00 per year (1.5 that for the whole 18 months), inclusive of sessional teaching amounts. The mentioned sessional teaching opportunities, subject to the University of Lethbridge faculty Association ( ULFA ) Academic Staff Collective Agreement. Access to the services of the University (e.g. library, information technologies) Office and meeting space on campus Opportunities to present and discuss research and to participate in Lab and departmental events and activities. Fellowship Eligibility Applicants must: Have fulfilled all degree requirements for their PhD before commencing the appointment, but no longer than five years prior to the start of the award (excepting career interruptions). Not hold a permanent faculty position or a faculty position leading to permanency. To Apply Please submit the following no later than October 15, 2026. Cover Letter Detailed CV Single-authored writing sample, written without the help of AI (please include an AI statement acknowledging that the sample was written by you, without the help of AI) Names and contact information for two references; Research statement (max. 2 pages, single-spaced): Select up to 3 research contributions that you consider to be your most important and describe their significance to the field. Describe the research you would like to conduct during the 18-month period of the Fellowship. Service statement (max 1 page, single spaced): Describe your organizational and/or editorial experience. Explain your motivation for applying for a Fellowship that concentrates on editorial activities. Statement addressing career interruptions (max. 1 page, single-spaced), if you are outside the 5-year eligibility window. Additional information Office of Post-Doctoral Affairs: https://www.ulethbridge.ca/research/postdoctoral-fellows . Position Category Other Faculty Faculty of Arts & Science Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/11/2026 Close Date 10/15/2026 Open Until Filled Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae References Research Statement Single-authored writing sample Optional Documents Additional Documents Additional Document #2 Additional Document 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/8841": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant (Research) - Full Fixed",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant (Research) - Full Fixed Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant (Research) - Full Fixed Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Assistant (Research) - Full Fixed About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Tenure Information Not Applicable Position Details We’re Hiring: Graduate Instructional Assistant – Graduate Peer Mentor Program & Orientation Want to create learning experiences that shape the next generation of graduate leaders? The School of Graduate Studies is looking for a Graduate Instructional Assistant to design interactive, engaging training for our Graduate Peer Mentor Program and review our orientation modules for the School of Graduate Studies. What you’ll do: Build and review online modules in Moodle and Arise. Turn a three-term mentorship curriculum into interactive, reflective, and scenario-based learning. Collaborate with graduate staff, mentors, and experts to ensure content is accurate, inclusive, and aligned with holistic development principles. Ensure our Graduate Studies Orientation ( GSO ) Modules are up-to-date. What we’re looking for: Experience in instructional design, e-learning, and adult learning. Skilled with Moodle and simulation-based learning (Arise preferred). Creative, collaborative, and passionate about graduate student success. Apply now – help us empower new graduate students at the beginning of their studies and mentors to guide peers academically, professionally, and personally! Please note: Only registered University of Lethbridge graduate students are eligible to apply for this posting. Graduate Assistant wages will be paid according to Schedule A of the ULGSA Collective Agreement. Position Category Graduate Assistant Faculty Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 12/10/2025 Close Date 01/04/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/19/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 04/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9294": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | SAMP Clerkship Coordinator (Full-time, Term)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | SAMP Clerkship Coordinator (Full-time, Term) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help SAMP Clerkship Coordinator (Full-time, Term) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title SAMP Clerkship Coordinator (Full-time, Term) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The Southern Alberta Medical Program is inviting applications for a Clerkship Coordinator (Program Administration 9). This is an AUPE full-time, 18-month term position that provides advisory, administrative, logistical, and program delivery assistance to SAMP leadership, preceptors, students (internal and external), and the Director of Clerkship for the delivery of the Undergraduate Medical Education ( UME ) curriculum for the Medical Doctor Program. The Clerkship Coordinator will: Act as a primary contact for information regarding scheduling and coordinating for Clerkship. Coordinate rotations, selection, and services in the SAMP UME office. Collaborate with UofC UME and Distributed Learning and Rural Initiatives ( DLRI ) to maintain course information, preceptor recruitment, and dissemination of information as required to staff, faculty, and students. Liaise with scheduling administrators across hospital disciplines, specialty offices, and clinical environments throughout Southern Alberta. Work as part of a team to support the day-to-day management of the SAMP clerkship by monitoring work flow, working with the SAMP leadership to ensure quality and accreditation standards are being met and contributing to developing action plans, with the Director, that meet program goals. This in-person position is at ULethbridge main campus, with occasional travel to the UCalgary campus and/or surrounding communities in Southern Alberta. Position Qualifications Post Secondary Diploma in Admin or a minimum of 3 years experience in project management. Strong collaboration skills, including the ability to interact with faculty, students, colleagues, and external stakeholders in a professional and courteous manner. Advanced knowledge of Microsoft applications. Excellent analytical and problem skills are essential. A valid unrestricted Class 5 Driver’s License with no more than 6 demerits and submission of a motor vehicle record (driver abstract) dated within 3 months of the posting close is required. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $5,000.00 - $5,589.00 monthly Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $5,000.00 - $6,177.00 monthly (AUPE - Grade 9) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/18/2026 Close Date 09/02/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 09/14/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 03/21/2028 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/8910": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Health Sciences - Nursing Sessional Instructor",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Health Sciences - Nursing Sessional Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Health Sciences - Nursing Sessional Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Health Sciences - Nursing Sessional Instructor About the University It’s your time to shine! Work where the world comes to create, discover and learn. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions. With more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students, two campuses (Lethbridge and Calgary), seven faculties and schools, and more than 2,500 employees, ULethbridge is Lethbridge’s second largest employer. Faculty and staff come together to contribute, each in their own way, to establishing ULethbridge as Canada’s destination university. In 2022, Lethbridge was recognized as one of Canada’s top small cities. Rank Tenure Information Position Details If you are open to innovation and committed to the creation of an environment that excites and ignites learning, we welcome your application. The Faculty of Health Sciences is an open, fair, honest, caring and collaborative community that strives to provide a rich education grounded in real world practice, drawing from the knowledge and expertise of multiple health disciplines. Position The Faculty of Health Sciences at the University of Lethbridge invites applications for sessional (part-time) instructors to teach 6 and/or 12 week clinical courses in the Fall, Spring and Summer semesters . Qualifications The successful candidates must be regulated members, in good standing, with the College of Registered Nurses of Alberta ( CRNA ). The candidates will also have at least five years of nursing practice in acute medical, and surgical settings. Applicants must have a Baccalaureate degree in nursing. The ideal candidate will also possess excellent communication, mentorship, and organizational skills, and maintain excellent working relationships with all nursing faculty, students, members of the University community and our service delivery partners. Candidates must demonstrate leadership in professional nursing practice in interdisciplinary settings . A thorough and current knowledge of nursing skills, procedures, and equipment related to nursing practice settings is required. Previous teaching experience is preferred. Academic Setting The CASN accredited four-year BN and 23-month BN After-Degree programs are offered in collaboration with Lethbridge College within the Nursing Education in Southwestern Alberta ( NESA ) Programs. Students practice in rural and urban settings including institutional and community locations. The University of Lethbridge has a reputation for providing a high-quality education and has been rated #1 for research activities among institutions of our size in Canada. The university website contains more information about our institution. To view additional information about the Faculty of Health Sciences, please visit our website at www.uleth.ca/hlsc . Remuneration You will receive an excellent salary commensurate with your experience, an annual professional development allowance, as well as a benefit package, including a tuition benefit for University of Lethbridge programming, and relocation assistance. Please visit The University of Lethbridge website to view the economic benefits package outlined in the Academic Staff Collective Agreement, https://www.ulethbridge.ca/hr/university-lethbridge-faculty-association-ulfa-faculty-handbook . Employment Equity In accordance with Canadian Immigration Regulation, first preference will be given to Canadian citizens and permanent residents of Canada. The University is an inclusive and equitable campus encouraging applications from qualified women and men including persons with disabilities, members of visible minorities, and Aboriginal persons. All positions are subject to Board approval. How to Apply All applications must be submitted online and must include a cover letter, contact information for three academic references who will be asked to provide reference letters, a detailed curriculum-vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness. Referees will be contacted directly, with information on how to submit their reference letters; the application submission will automatically trigger this request to your references. For enquiries about this position, please contact Pam Smith, Administrative Manager, Faculty of Health Sciences, at pamela.smith4@uleth.ca Position Category Faculty Faculty of Health Sciences Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 06/28/2023 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9297": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Finance System Implementation Manager (Full-time, Continuing) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Finance System Implementation Manager (Full-time, Continuing) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Finance System Implementation Manager (Full-time, Continuing) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, We Shape Tomorrow The Future Systems and Processes ( FSP ) program is a multi-year initiative to modernize the university’s finance, human resource, and student information processes and systems ( ERP / SIS ) and facilitate the adoption and successful implementation of a next-generation platform for long-term operational excellence that best supports our diverse community. As we create the capacity to support the program, some postings will be for roles within the project itself, while others will be hired to fulfill operational responsibilities so that experienced professionals can focus on planning and implementing the critical improvements that this program will deliver. The backfill positions, along with FSP program-specific positions, are funded entirely through dedicated project reserves, underscoring our commitment to responsible financial stewardship and long-term planning. Position Details The Finance System Implementation Manager will work collaboratively with a cross-functional team to support the modernization, integration, and implementation of finance modules as part of a larger enterprise resource planning ( ERP ) implementation project. This role will contribute to improving operational efficiency and productivity, strengthening internal controls, and advancing Financial Services’ strategic and operational objectives. This is a full-time continuing position reporting to the Director, Financial Systems Support & Development, with a start date as soon as possible. Primary duties and responsibilities include working closely with ERP modernization and implementation project teams while representing Financial Services in the following key areas: Supporting project planning activities, including the development of finance project timelines, resource allocation plans, and project deliverables to ensure work is completed on time and within scope; providing leadership and guidance to Finance employees involved in ERP implementation activities, as required. Analyzing finance processes, requirements, and workflows to identify deficiencies and opportunities for improvement; collaborating with finance stakeholders to redesign and optimize processes that align with the capabilities of a modernized ERP system. Coordinating with Information Technology teams, external vendors, and technical consultants to configure financial modules (e.g., General Ledger, Accounts Payable/Receivable, and Asset Management) and ensure seamless integration with new and existing systems. Overseeing financial data management activities, including data cleanup, retention planning, and data migration, while ensuring data integrity, consistency, and accuracy throughout the transition. Coordinating system testing and quality assurance activities to ensure implemented solutions meet business requirements, operational needs, and compliance standards. Leading the development and delivery of training materials and user training programs; providing regular project updates; communicating project impacts, decisions, and changes; and managing stakeholder expectations throughout the implementation process. The incumbent will serve as a change agent and key member of the project team, supporting organizational readiness and user adoption of finance systems while building and maintaining strong working relationships with finance leadership, project collaborators, system user groups, and other stakeholders. The University of Lethbridge is undertaking a job classification and compensation review for Administrative Professional Officer ( APO ) positions. As such, the salary range currently assigned for this position may be adjusted as a result of this project. Position Qualifications Success in this role requires strong risk management, problem-solving, and relationship-management capabilities, including the ability to proactively identify, assess, and manage project risks and issues; anticipate potential challenges; and develop effective mitigation strategies that support project objectives, timelines, and successful outcomes. The ideal candidate will possess a Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Information Technology, or a related field, along with a minimum of five years of experience leading or supporting complex, large-scale system implementation projects. Experience with enterprise ERP platforms such as Banner (Ellucian), PeopleSoft, Workday, or similar systems is required. Experience with finance system implementations, business process redesign, data migration, and stakeholder engagement is highly desirable. Familiarity with the post-secondary education sector is preferred. A CPA designation (or progress toward completion) and/or a Project Management Professional ( PMP ) designation would be considered an asset. The successful candidate will be required to provide a satisfactory Criminal Record Check. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $77,111.09 - $97,005.51 annually Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $77,111.09 - $116,899.94 annually (APO - Grade 4) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group APO Position Category Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/20/2026 Close Date 09/27/2026 Open Until Filled Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9160": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Standardized Patient, Southern Alberta Medical Program (Casual) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Standardized Patient, Southern Alberta Medical Program (Casual) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Standardized Patient, Southern Alberta Medical Program (Casual) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details Are you interested in participating in training future physicians? This is a casual role with opportunities to participate on Tuesday afternoons throughout the year and occasional exam blocks. This role may involve role play for communications, being a human subject for non invasive physical exam procedures and providing feedback to students and faculty where appropriate. Ability to provide sensitive, critical intuitive verbal and written feedback following the established model when required and adhere to strict guidelines of standardization are essential. Summary of Key Responsibilities (job functions include but are not limited to): Mental and physical stamina to reproduce exacting scenarios up to 8 or more times a day for some of the exams or courses. Able to provide sensitive, critical intuitive verbal and written feedback to faculty when required as this is utilized in the evaluation of student performance. Adhere to strict guidelines of standardization, from the first encounter to the last and with other SPs of the same case; to maintain consistency and fairness for examinations. Maintain confidentiality of information related to student performance and feedback evaluations. Apply developed knowledge and expertise successfully to roles & responsibilities and acts as a key resource to others. Role play for communications. Provide feedback to students and faculty, where appropriate. Human subject for non-evasive physical exam procedures. May be required to role play in large class setting to facilitate lectures. Starting Hourly Wage Range: $23.96 – $26.50 Full Hourly Wage Range: $23.96 – $29.04 Position Qualifications Experience in acting with post-secondary education in this field. Ability to use improvisational skills, as cases require non-text experience. Ability to memorize large amounts of complex information related to personality traits, behavioral symptoms and disease entities. Ability to accurately, convincingly and consistently interpret and present symptoms and/or information, as cued by students in a simulated situation. Ability, when requested, to provide consistent, objective and focused feedback and evaluation to students in a simulated and/or testing environment within the established feedback model. Required to maintain confidentiality of records and information. Two to four years’ experience in related position preferred. Must be able to negotiate personal boundaries and request assistance if needed. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 05/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 07/13/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 12/31/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9304": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Security Representative (Full-Time, Continuing) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Security Representative (Full-Time, Continuing) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Security Representative (Full-Time, Continuing) About the University It’s your time to shine! Work where the world comes to create, discover and learn. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions. With more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students, two campuses (Lethbridge and Calgary), seven faculties and schools, and more than 2,500 employees, ULethbridge is Lethbridge’s second largest employer. Faculty and staff come together to contribute, each in their own way, to establishing ULethbridge as Canada’s destination university. In 2022, Lethbridge was recognized as one of Canada’s top small cities. Position Details The University of Lethbridge is seeking a Full-time, Continuing Security Representative. Security Representatives provide 24/7 coverage on a negotiated rotating 12-hour shift pattern. Duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to patrols and investigative work focused on enhancing the safety and security of persons, buildings, property, and the environment, traffic control, and assisting the campus community where appropriate or as required. Employees shall be eligible for applicable premiums as outlined in the AUPE Collective Agreement. Position Qualifications The successful candidate will be required to provide: A satisfactory Criminal Record Check, including a Vulnerable Sector check. A valid unrestricted Class 5 Driver’s License with no more than 6 demerits and submission of a motor vehicle record (driver abstract) dated within 3 months of the posting close is required. A valid First Aid / CPR Certificate. A valid Alberta Security Services License in accordance with the Alberta Security Services and Investigators Act. The ideal candidate will have: Experience in a security related field, uniformed services industries, or equivalent training and/or experience. Demonstrated understanding and knowledge of the Alberta Security Services and Investigators Act. The ability to physically conduct patrols for extended periods of time in varying conditions. The ability to interact with various individuals often in difficult situations while assisting and maintaining a professional demeanor. Working knowledge in Office 365, alarm management, access control, and property management programs. Knowledge of fire prevention methods and response procedures. An understanding of Standard Operating Procedures formats. The ability to to work independently and successfully in a team environment. Experience in writing reports as required. Strong communication skills both verbal and written. Working knowledge in closed-circuit television ( CCTV ) programs. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $4,390.00 - $4,884.00 monthly Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $4,390.00 - $5,378.00 monthly (AUPE - Grade 8) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/26/2026 Close Date 09/02/2026 Open Until Filled Desired Start Date 09/03/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9206": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Liberal Education Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Liberal Education Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Liberal Education Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Liberal Education Assistant Professor About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. The University of Lethbridge is a comprehensive and research-intensive university founded on the principles of liberal education where inspired scholars integrate research and creative activity with teaching. Our University’s Blackfoot name is Iniskim, meaning Sacred Buffalo Stone. Founded in 1967 on traditional Blackfoot land, it is a place where student engagement in learning, creative activities, and research takes place every day. With campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary, the University of Lethbridge offers more than 150 undergraduate and 60 graduate programs in the Faculties of Arts & Science, Education, Fine Arts, Health Sciences, the Schools of Liberal Education and Graduate Studies, and the Dhillon School of Business, to more than 8,000 students. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Tenure Information Position Details Position Description The School of Liberal Education at the University of Lethbridge invites applications for a tenure-track position in Liberal Education at the rank of Assistant Professor with a start date of January 1, 2027, subject to budgetary approval. A start date of July 1, 2027 is also possible. Hiring salary will be in the range of $86,470 to $98,000 per year, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The successful candidate will be expected to undertake interdisciplinary teaching and research in the School of Liberal Education. The successful candidate will develop and teach courses addressing a broad range of quantitative or science-related topics and principles to a wide variety of undergraduate students with different majors. The successful candidate must hold a Ph.D. (or a nearly completed Ph.D. with a defence date scheduled) and have a strong quantitative background. A graduate degree in a STEM discipline or in Health Sciences would be an asset. A clear demonstration of teaching proficiency as the primary instructor in one or more undergraduate courses is essential. The School is particularly interested in applicants with a background or interest in Indigenous Science, land-based learning, climate science, or environmental science. Required Documents An application should include: A letter of application expressing interest in the position that articulates i) the candidate’s understanding of liberal education and how it relates to their potential contributions to this position; and ii) the candidate’s commitment to collegiality. A curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy and approach (not exceeding two pages) A statement of research interests (not exceeding two pages) Contact information for two referees who can speak to the candidate’s achievement in or potential to contribute to teaching and research in the School of Liberal Education The Committee will begin reviewing applications on September 15, 2026. For inquiries about the position, please contact Dr. Harold Jansen, Dean, School of Liberal Education at libadmin@uleth.ca. While all applications will be considered, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. Understanding that career interruptions can have an impact on a candidate’s record of achievement, we encourage applicants to explain in their applications any impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The School of Liberal Education Founded in 2017, the School of Liberal Education is a small unit of faculty members and instructors at the University of Lethbridge who are distinguished by their commitment to interdisciplinary teaching and research. The School’s academic staff teach a variety of undergraduate courses in liberal education to a diverse student body. Faculty members are expected to develop and maintain research programs. There are opportunities to collaborate with other faculty members across the University. The City of Lethbridge The city of Lethbridge has over 100,000 people and is located in Southern Alberta, not far from the Rocky Mountains and the U.S. border. Lethbridge enjoys a sunny, dry climate that is surprisingly mild, has excellent cultural and recreational amenities, and offers attractive economic conditions including affordable housing. For more information see the City’s website at www.lethbridge.ca. Position Category Research Faculty Faculty of Education Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/07/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/01/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interest Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). I authorize the University of Lethbridge to disclose the personal information submitted as my application package to the search committee and members of the department for the purpose of administering the selection process for this position. This consent is valid for the period of one year from the date the application information is submitted. I agree I dont agree The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9309": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Housing Student Mail Clerk (Casual) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Housing Student Mail Clerk (Casual) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Housing Student Mail Clerk (Casual) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The Housing Student Mail Clerk is responsible for the accurate receiving, sorting, and distribution of resident mail and parcel deliveries. This position supports effective communication within the Housing community by maintaining bulletin boards, posting approved notices and promotional materials, and assisting with general residence administrative tasks as assigned. Key Responsibilities: Receive, sort, and distribute resident mail and packages accurately and confidentially. Notify residents of package deliveries in a timely manner. Maintain organized mailroom and package storage areas. Update residence bulletin boards with current information, notices, and event promotions. Post and remove approved posters and signage throughout residence facilities. Provide courteous and professional customer service to residents, staff, and visitors. Assist with other administrative and operational duties as assigned by Housing Services. The successful applicant will arrange work hours in consultation with the Housing Associate Director of Admin and Building Operations. Training will be provided, and a detailed job description will be available to the successful candidate. Starting wage: $18.80 per hour. Position Qualifications Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accuracy when handling mail and packages. Excellent organizational and time-management skills. Ability to provide friendly, professional customer service to residents and staff. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work independently and take initiative while following established procedures. Demonstrated reliability, responsibility, and punctuality. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion when handling resident information. Basic computer proficiency, including email and web-based applications. Ability to safely lift and move mail and parcels as required. Current University of Lethbridge student, preferably residing in Housing. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/27/2026 Close Date 09/03/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 09/14/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9229": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | SharePoint Analyst (Full-time, Term) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help SharePoint Analyst (Full-time, Term) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title SharePoint Analyst (Full-time, Term) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The University of Lethbridge is seeking a SharePoint Analyst to assist with the planning and implementation of campus-wide electronic records management initiatives using Microsoft SharePoint Online and Microsoft Purview. This is a two-year (2) term position located at our Lethbridge campus. Position Overview: As the SharePoint Analyst, you will play a central role in advancing the university’s use of SharePoint Online and Microsoft Purview for records and information management. Working with a small team of technical specialists and process owners, you will help translate business and records management needs into practical configuration, administration, and support activities within SharePoint Online. The position will also support the planned use of Microsoft Purview capabilities, including sensitivity labels, retention policies, and retention labels across administrative and research areas. This position reports to the Director of Infrastructure and works closely with the Records and Information Manager, Security and Systems teams, as well as academic and administrative units. Key Responsibilities: Understand Business Requirements Work to understand the needs of the business and match them with capabilities of the Purview and SharePoint Online applications to optimize the management of electronic documents. Implement Electronic Records Management Serve as the technical expert for SharePoint Online and Microsoft Purview to assist in developing an effective electronic document records management program with a small team. Leverage and Grow the Usage of Tools Assist users to leverage tools such as SharePoint Online and Microsoft Purview to manage the lifecycle of digital records. Configure SharePoint Online for efficient and appropriate record storage. Create and administer sensitivity labels, retention policies and labels to manage data. This will help teams to protect sensitive information and ensure the university meets its legal and regulatory obligations. Configure SharePoint Online Assist business users in configuring document repositories within SharePoint sites to conform electronic records management program once developed. The University of Lethbridge is undertaking a job classification and compensation review for Administrative Professional Officer ( APO ) positions. As such, the salary range currently assigned for this position may be adjusted as a result of this project. Position Qualifications Education: University degree in a relevant field (e.g. data science, computer science, etc). Experience: Experience administering and configuring a Microsoft SharePoint Online tenant is required. Experience with Microsoft Purview would be ideal. Experience in a post-secondary environment is preferred. Skills: 2+ years of experience configuring and managing a SharePoint Online tenant as an administrator Experience working with records management and electronic document management system implementations Familiarity with Microsoft Purview or other Microsoft 365 compliance features would be considered an asset Excellent planning, coordination, and interpersonal skills Strong written and verbal communication Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $66,716.84 - $83,930.19 annually Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $66,716.84 - $101,143.54 annually (APO - Grade 3) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group APO Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 09/01/2028 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9313": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Sports Performance Coach (Full-time, Recurring Limited Term) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Sports Performance Coach (Full-time, Recurring Limited Term) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Sports Performance Coach (Full-time, Recurring Limited Term) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The Athletics & Recreation Department is seeking a Sport Performance Coach to support the development and delivery of high-performance training programs for all varsity, club, and youth sport athletes. In this role, you will assist in designing and implementing year-round strength and conditioning programs for male and female athletes, including in-season, off-season, and pre-season training. Programs will reflect research-driven practices and align with our country’s long-term Athletic/Fitness Development Model. You’ll be responsible for writing and supervising training plans, conducting athlete testing, monitoring performance, and maintaining detailed training records. You will also support the coordination of club sports and youth training programs, ensuring consistency and quality across all levels. These programs are a key part of our department’s revenue generation. Additionally, you will collaborate closely with coaches and training staff to implement performance monitoring technology, including Athlete Monitoring software and TitanGPS, to track and enhance athlete performance. Please note that a strong internal candidate will be applying for this position. Position Qualifications The ideal candidate will hold a Bachelor’s degree in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, or a related field, with a minimum of three years of experience in strength and conditioning. A CSCS certification (or equivalent) is required, along with Standard First Aid and CPR / AED certification. The successful candidate will have a strong understanding of sport performance and the training demands of national, provincial, and university-level athletes. They will be skilled in applying sport science principles, including the use of data collection and analysis to enhance athlete performance. This position will require a satisfactory Criminal Record and Vulnerable Sector Check. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $5,214.00 - $5,904.00 monthly Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $5,214.00 - $6,593.00 monthly (AUPE - Grade 11) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/02/2026 Close Date 09/09/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 09/10/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 03/31/2029 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9242": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Arts &amp; Science - Assistant Professor (Psychology)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Arts &amp; Science - Assistant Professor (Psychology) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty of Arts & Science - Assistant Professor (Psychology) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Faculty of Arts & Science - Assistant Professor (Psychology) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Position Details The Department of Psychology invites applications for a Tenure-Track position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin 1st July 2027, subject to budgetary approval. Hiring salary will be in the range of $89,064 and $102,100 per year, with starting salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. We are seeking a colleague whose teaching and research focus on any aspect of human cognition, social psychology, or individual differences. Outstanding candidates should also be able to teach a range of junior- and senior-level undergraduate courses in their area of expertise. They will establish and sustain an independent, externally funded research program, demonstrate excellence in engaging and inspiring undergraduate and graduate students, and contribute actively to departmental programs and curriculum development. It is imperative that the successful applicant holds a Ph.D. and at least one graduate degree in Psychology. Our Team: The Department of Psychology has an enthusiastic group of faculty members with diverse and active research programs. Our interests range across various areas of experimental, social and forensic psychology, to sociocultural behaviour in humans and other animals, and aspects of animal communication. The department has an established graduate program and a thriving undergraduate student culture, encouraged through faculty involvement. Our University: The University of Lethbridge (uLethbridge) is a comprehensive and research-intensive university founded on the principles of liberal education where inspired scholars integrate research and creative activity with teaching. Our University’s Blackfoot name is Iniskim, meaning Sacred Buffalo Stone. Founded in 1967 on traditional Blackfoot land, it is a place where student engagement in learning, creative activities, and research takes place every day. With campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary, uLethbridge offers more than 150 undergraduate and 60 graduate programs in the Faculties of Arts & Science, Education, Fine Arts, Health Sciences, the Schools of Liberal Education and Graduate Studies, and the Dhillon School of Business. Together, these programs serve more than 8,500 students. Our Values: The university recognizes that diversity enriches our campus and our community and is fundamental to excellence in teaching, learning, and research. The university as a whole embraces equity as a core value to be truly inclusive of the communities of which we are a part, and this requires ongoing intentional and systemic action. Through recruitment and support of individuals who further enhance our diversity, the University strives to create a diverse and inclusive community where students, faculty and staff feel welcome, are treated equitably, and can thrive. Our City: Living and benefiting from Blackfoot Confederacy’s traditional territory, Iniskim (uLethbridge) is direct neighbours with Kainai Nation , the largest reserve in Canada. We acknowledge and deeply appreciate the Siksikaitsitapi peoples’ connection to their traditional territory and honour the traditions of people who have cared for this land since time immemorial. Home to more than 100,000 people, Lethbridge is a place where ideas grow. It is a culturally vibrant city with a flourishing arts scene and an active social calendar. We boast stunning scenery, four distinct seasons, spectacular sunrises and glowing sunsets that illuminate Alberta’s big sky. The University sits on the beautiful coulees, looking down on the Old Man River. Lethbridge is only two hours from Calgary’s International Airport and a short drive to the mountainous Waterton Lakes National Park. Looking for a centre with a lower cost of living than many other Canadian cities? See the Canadian Real Estate Association national price map to compare average Canadian housing prices. Lethbridge is an affordable city, with many beautiful neighborhoods on both sides of the coulees and well-planned parks connected via walking and biking paths Our Application Process: All applications must be submitted online, and include a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching interests and philosophy, outlines of courses previously taught, a statement of research program, teaching evaluations (if available), and the contact information for three references (references will be contacted directly for short-listed candidates). The initial deadline for applications is 28 September 2026 , but the position will remain open until the short-list of candidates is finalized. For enquiries about the position, please contact Dr. Jean-Baptiste Leca, Chair, Department of Psychology, jeanbaptiste.leca@uleth.ca Position Category Faculty Faculty of Arts & Science Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 07/01/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Outlines References Letter of Application Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Teaching/Research Interests Statement of Research Program Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). I authorize the University of Lethbridge to disclose the personal information submitted as my application package to the search committee and members of the department for the purpose of administering the selection process for this position. This consent is valid for the period of one year from the application date the information is submitted. I agree I don't Agree The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
